{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017EVzGFCi2JtEuzdD71prkA","type":"tool_result","content":"8:#   (rabadon-gated, unix socket) plus a thin client removes exactly that, so\n15:#   written under reports/R7/ or this script fails — see GOAL 4.\n22:# reports/R1.3/accept.sh (GOAL 4): a COPY of the shipped gate source is patched\n33:# The same reasoning is why GOAL 2c exists. R1.3 closed with a residual ~4%\n48:AUDITBIN=\"$ROOT/native/rabadon-audit\"   # GOAL 3 requires it; see the CEVAP block there\n60:# that loop, with the socket appearing ~300 ms later. So the loop was timing a\n61:# race, not testing a daemon. The requirement does NOT loosen: the socket is\n66:sock_bekle(){ # $1 = socket path; 0 if it appeared inside the cap (10 s)\n85:head_ \"GOAL 1 — the daemon and the thin client exist at all\"\n86:# Three separate claims. A binary that exists but never binds a socket is not a\n94:  note \"this is the whole speed half of R7; without it GOALs 2 and 3 measure nothing\"\n101:  pass \"1b $GSRC binds and listens on a unix socket (a daemon, not a one-shot)\"\n107:# The client must PREFER the socket and FALL BACK to today's in-process path.\n112:  [ -f \"$c\" ] && grep -q 'RABADON_GATED_SOCK\\|rabadon-gated.sock\\|gated.sock' \"$c\" && CSRC=\"$c\" && break\n115:  pass \"1c a thin client path referencing the daemon socket exists ($CSRC)\"\n117:  fail \"1c nothing in the gate reaches for a daemon socket — there is no thin client\"\n121:head_ \"GOAL 2 — with the daemon up, the gate's median is under 1 ms (in-process)\"\n128:SOCK=\"$W/rabadon-gated.sock\"\n134:  sock_bekle \"$SOCK\" && DAEMON_UP=1\n135:  if [ \"$DAEMON_UP\" = 1 ]; then pass \"2a the daemon started and its socket is listening\"\n136:  else fail \"2a rabadon-gated did not produce a listening socket at $SOCK\"; note \"$(tail -2 \"$W/gated.log\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; fi\n190:    DPID=$!; sock_bekle \"$SOCK\"\n211:    # R1.3 GOAL 6: two sandboxes, one seeded to 50 events and one to 400, BOTH\n250:head_ \"GOAL 3 — with the daemon down, behaviour is byte-identical to today\"\n261:  # that buys that signal back is the in-arm audit. Without the binary GOAL 3\n266:  note \"GOAL 3 blanks the chain's prev field and pays for it with an INTACT audit\"\n269:  DEAD=\"$W/definitely-not-a-socket.sock\"\n296:  # the WRONG line would slip through. So GOAL 3 now runs rabadon-audit inside\n357:head_ \"GOAL 4 — the harness is named, exactly, with its commit\"\n387:head_ \"GOAL 5 — the raw run lands here, and can be re-run\"\n431:head_ \"GOAL 6 — the five numbers, each of them, from the raw data\"\n492:head_ \"GOAL 7 — the falsification conditions are checkable, and checked\"\n523:head_ \"GOAL 8 — nothing already standing fell over\"","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f40cbadd-2bac-41b8-9a9c-9348aaba08b1","uuid":"01ab247d-a019-4d68-ab11-4b4cb69043f2","timestamp":"2026-08-24T12:49:05.657Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"8:#   (rabadon-gated, unix socket) plus a thin client removes exactly that, so\n15:#   written under reports/R7/ or this script fails — see GOAL 4.\n22:# reports/R1.3/accept.sh (GOAL 4): a COPY of the shipped gate source is patched\n33:# The same reasoning is why GOAL 2c exists. R1.3 closed with a residual ~4%\n48:AUDITBIN=\"$ROOT/native/rabadon-audit\"   # GOAL 3 requires it; see the CEVAP block there\n60:# that loop, with the socket appearing ~300 ms later. So the loop was timing a\n61:# race, not testing a daemon. The requirement does NOT loosen: the socket is\n66:sock_bekle(){ # $1 = socket path; 0 if it appeared inside the cap (10 s)\n85:head_ \"GOAL 1 — the daemon and the thin client exist at all\"\n86:# Three separate claims. A binary that exists but never binds a socket is not a\n94:  note \"this is the whole speed half of R7; without it GOALs 2 and 3 measure nothing\"\n101:  pass \"1b $GSRC binds and listens on a unix socket (a daemon, not a one-shot)\"\n107:# The client must PREFER the socket and FALL BACK to today's in-process path.\n112:  [ -f \"$c\" ] && grep -q 'RABADON_GATED_SOCK\\|rabadon-gated.sock\\|gated.sock' \"$c\" && CSRC=\"$c\" && break\n115:  pass \"1c a thin client path referencing the daemon socket exists ($CSRC)\"\n117:  fail \"1c nothing in the gate reaches for a daemon socket — there is no thin client\"\n121:head_ \"GOAL 2 — with the daemon up, the gate's median is under 1 ms (in-process)\"\n128:SOCK=\"$W/rabadon-gated.sock\"\n134:  sock_bekle \"$SOCK\" && DAEMON_UP=1\n135:  if [ \"$DAEMON_UP\" = 1 ]; then pass \"2a the daemon started and its socket is listening\"\n136:  else fail \"2a rabadon-gated did not produce a listening socket at $SOCK\"; note \"$(tail -2 \"$W/gated.log\" 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')\"; fi\n190:    DPID=$!; sock_bekle \"$SOCK\"\n211:    # R1.3 GOAL 6: two sandboxes, one seeded to 50 events and one to 400, BOTH\n250:head_ \"GOAL 3 — with the daemon down, behaviour is byte-identical to today\"\n261:  # that buys that signal back is the in-arm audit. Without the binary GOAL 3\n266:  note \"GOAL 3 blanks the chain's prev field and pays for it with an INTACT audit\"\n269:  DEAD=\"$W/definitely-not-a-socket.sock\"\n296:  # the WRONG line would slip through. So GOAL 3 now runs rabadon-audit inside\n357:head_ \"GOAL 4 — the harness is named, exactly, with its commit\"\n387:head_ \"GOAL 5 — the raw run lands here, and can be re-run\"\n431:head_ \"GOAL 6 — the five numbers, each of them, from the raw data\"\n492:head_ \"GOAL 7 — the falsification conditions are checkable, and checked\"\n523:head_ \"GOAL 8 — nothing already standing fell over\"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
