{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMboP7FSCSv68ZpQsDG2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NtmKrXdE6hVrNsZMwFptSs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git log --oneline -1 -- native/sock_path_test.sh; echo \"--- doc 60-72 ---\"; sed -n '60,72p' KOSU-RABADON-2.md; echo \"--- accept.sh refs to sock_path_test ---\"; grep -rn 'sock_path_test' reports/ native/*.sh 2>/dev/null | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3220,"cache_read_input_tokens":32839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3220},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f40cbadd-2bac-41b8-9a9c-9348aaba08b1","uuid":"dc7551ba-6968-4bc7-a4dc-4400aa39ff79","request_id":"req_011CeMboNAwL8kcb62C56y7C"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NtmKrXdE6hVrNsZMwFptSs","type":"tool_result","content":"7d344ee native: the socket-path-length check that was claimed to exist — RED\n--- doc 60-72 ---\ngerekçe `reports/R7/HARNESS.md`. R7'de operatöre açık soru KALMADI.\n**Yasa 7:** iki kol farkı gürültü içinde kalırsa \"kurtarır\" YAYINLANMAZ;\nmetrik + minimum örnek sayısı koşudan ÖNCE reports/R7/ altına (ön-kayıt).\n**Mimari kural — soket yolu (24.08):** daemon soketi REPO/WORKTREE içine\nAÇILMAZ. sockaddr_un.sun_path tavanı Linux 108 / macOS 104 bayttır; derin\nworktree yolu + soket adı bunu sessizce aşar, bind() ENAMETOOLONG ile düşer\nve ajan bunu kod hatası sanıp C++'ı boşuna yeniden yazar. Soket yolu KISA ve\nMUTLAK: `${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/rabadon-$UID.sock`, 0600 izin; yol uzunluğu\nsınırı R7 testinde assert edilir. Değerlendiren bu kuralı ilk R7 talimatına\naynen taşır.\n\n### A2. R8 — yayın (bloklu: \"yeşil main\" kararı OPERATÖR'e)\n- npm 404; package.json 0.2.3, tag'siz. Kabul: `npm view rabadon version` sayı\n--- accept.sh refs to sock_path_test ---\nreports/R7/CHALLENGE-3.md:59:+sınırı `native/sock_path_test.sh`'ta assert edilir (24.08'e kadar HİÇBİR\nreports/R7/DENEMELER.md:339:Önce KIRMIZI test (`native/sock_path_test.sh`, 1 ok / 2 FAILED), sonra ayrı\nreports/kosu/11.out.raw:8:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WszT2ejiaM9NyN99Awt1Aa\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# CHALLENGE 3 — KOSU-RABADON-2.md A1 claims a test that does not exist\\n2\\t\\n3\\tStatus: OPEN. Raised tur 8 (2026-08-24). A challenged step is treated as RED.\\n4\\tThis challenge does NOT touch the invariants block. It needs a human-approved\\n5\\tdiff to KOSU-RABADON-2.md in its own commit.\\n6\\t\\n7\\t## The claim\\n8\\t\\n9\\t`KOSU-RABADON-2.md:63-69`, the \\\"Mimari kural — soket yolu (24.08)\\\" block, ends:\\n10\\t\\n11\\t> Soket yolu KISA ve MUTLAK: `${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/rabadon-$UID.sock`, 0600\\n12\\t> izin; **yol uzunluğu sınırı R7 testinde assert edilir.**\\n13\\t\\n14\\t(\\\"the path length limit is asserted in the R7 test\\\")\\n15\\t\\n16\\t## The evidence that it is false\\n17\\t\\n18\\t```\\n19\\t$ grep -niE 'sun_path|ENAMETOOLONG|104|108|path.*(length|len|too long)' reports/R7/accept.sh\\n20\\t>>> no match\\n21\\t```\\n22\\t\\n23\\t`reports/R7/accept.sh` contains no socket-path-length assertion of any kind.\\n24\\tIts only length-related work is GOAL 2c, which is about *ledger* length\\n25\\tdependence (`accept.sh:145`, `210-241`) — a different quantity entirely.\\n26\\t\\n27\\tNor is the assertion anywhere else: a grep for `sun_path` / `ENAMETOOLONG`\\n28\\tacross `native/*.cpp`, `native/*.h` and `native/*.sh` finds the guard only\\n29\\tinside the product (`native/gated.cpp:157`, `native/gated_client.h:98`) and in\\n30\\tno test. `reports/R7/DENEMELER.md:113-114` measured one path once (79 bytes);\\n31\\tthat is a measurement, not a check, and it cannot fail.\\n32\\t\\n33\\tSo the document asserts that a risk is covered by a test, and it is not\\n34\\tcovered by anything. This is exactly the failure mode the architectural rule\\n35\\titself was written to prevent: an agent hits a truncated-path failure, believes\\n36\\ta test would have caught it, and looks for the bug in the C++.\\n37\\t\\n38\\t## Why it is not merely cosmetic\\n39\\t\\n40\\tThe unguarded path is reachable in this project's own reference environment.\\n41\\tA `mktemp -d` HOME — what the acceptance script itself uses — yields a\\n42\\t`sockPath` of ~85 bytes against a macOS cap of 104: **19 bytes of headroom,\\n43\\tunguarded**. And the consequence of overrunning it is not a clean failure; see\\n44\\tthe separate finding on `native/gate.cpp:721`, where truncation silently\\n45\\tconnects to a *different* socket and ships the ledger stream there.\\n46\\t\\n47\\t## Proposed diff (NOT applied — needs human approval)\\n48\\t\\n49\\tEither make the sentence true, or delete it. Making it true is preferred and\\n50\\tis the smaller change, because the test is worth having on its own merits:\\n51\\t\\n52\\t```diff\\n53\\t--- a/KOSU-RABADON-2.md\\n54\\t+++ b/KOSU-RABADON-2.md\\n55\\t@@ -66,8 +66,10 @@\\n56\\t MUTLAK: `${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/rabadon-$UID.sock`, 0600 izin; yol uzunluğu\\n57\\t-sınırı R7 testinde assert edilir. Değerlendiren bu kuralı ilk R7 talimatına\\n58\\t-aynen taşır.\\n59\\t+sınırı `native/sock_path_test.sh`'ta assert edilir (24.08'e kadar HİÇBİR\\n60\\t+testte assert EDİLMİYORDU — CHALLENGE-3). Test, kapasitenin aşıldığı durumda\\n61\\t+(a) kesik yola HİÇBİR bayt gitmediğini ve (b) sebebin stderr'e yazıldığını\\n62\\t+kanıtlar. Değerlendiren bu kuralı ilk R7 talimatına aynen taşır.\\n63\\t```\\n64\\t\\n65\\tThe maker of tur 8 did NOT apply this diff and did not edit KOSU-RABADON-2.md.\\n66\\tThe accompanying test is being written separately; until a human approves the\\n67\\tdiff above, the document and the tree still disagree, and this stays OPEN.\\n68\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f40cbadd-2bac-41b8-9a9c-9348aaba08b1\",\"uuid\":\"0d610e37-2ca3-4d20-97e4-513018fe2a2c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-24T12:49:00.253Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/reports/R7/CHALLENGE-3.md\",\"content\":\"# CHALLENGE 3 — KOSU-RABADON-2.md A1 claims a test that does not exist\\n\\nStatus: OPEN. Raised tur 8 (2026-08-24). A challenged step is treated as RED.\\nThis challenge does NOT touch the invariants block. It needs a human-approved\\ndiff to KOSU-RABADON-2.md in its own commit.\\n\\n## The claim\\n\\n`KOSU-RABADON-2.md:63-69`, the \\\"Mimari kural — soket yolu (24.08)\\\" block, ends:\\n\\n> Soket yolu KISA ve MUTLAK: `${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/rabadon-$UID.sock`, 0600\\n> izin; **yol uzunluğu sınırı R7 testinde assert edilir.**\\n\\n(\\\"the path length limit is asserted in the R7 test\\\")\\n\\n## The evidence that it is false\\n\\n```\\n$ grep -niE 'sun_path|ENAMETOOLONG|104|108|path.*(length|len|too long)' reports/R7/accept.sh\\n>>> no match\\n```\\n\\n`reports/R7/accept.sh` contains no socket-path-length assertion of any kind.\\nIts only length-related work is GOAL 2c, which is about *ledger* length\\ndependence (`accept.sh:145`, `210-241`) — a different quantity entirely.\\n\\nNor is the assertion anywhere else: a grep for `sun_path` / `ENAMETOOLONG`\\nacross `native/*.cpp`, `native/*.h` and `native/*.sh` finds the guard only\\ninside the product (`native/gated.cpp:157`, `native/gated_client.h:98`) and in\\nno test. `reports/R7/DENEMELER.md:113-114` measured one path once (79 bytes);\\nthat is a measurement, not a check, and it cannot fail.\\n\\nSo the document asserts that a risk is covered by a test, and it is not\\ncovered by anything. This is exactly the failure mode the architectural rule\\nitself was written to prevent: an agent hits a truncated-path failure, believes\\na test would have caught it, and looks for the bug in the C++.\\n\\n## Why it is not merely cosmetic\\n\\nThe unguarded path is reachable in this project's own reference environment.\\nA `mktemp -d` HOME — what the acceptance script itself uses — yields a\\n`sockPath` of ~85 bytes against a macOS cap of 104: **19 bytes of headroom,\\nunguarded**. And the consequence of overrunning it is not a clean failure; see\\nthe separate finding on `native/gate.cpp:721`, where truncation silently\\nconnects to a *different* socket and ships the ledger stream there.\\n\\n## Proposed diff (NOT applied — needs human approval)\\n\\nEither make the sentence true, or delete it. Making it true is preferred and\\nis the smaller change, because the test is worth having on its own merits:\\n\\n```diff\\n--- a/KOSU-RABADON-2.md\\n+++ b/KOSU-RABADON-2.md\\n@@ -66,8 +66,10 @@\\n MUTLAK: `${XDG_RUNTIME_DIR:-/tmp}/rabadon-$UID.sock`, 0600 izin; yol uzunluğu\\n-sınırı R7 testinde assert edilir. Değerlendiren bu kuralı ilk R7 talimatına\\n-aynen taşır.\\n+sınırı `native/sock_path_test.sh`'ta assert edilir (24.08'e kadar HİÇBİR\\n+testte assert EDİLMİYORDU — CHALLENGE-3). Test, kapasitenin aşıldığı durumda\\n+(a) kesik yola HİÇBİR bayt gitmediğini ve (b) sebebin stderr'e yazıldığını\\n+kanıtlar. Değerlendiren bu kuralı ilk R7 talimatına aynen taşır.\\n```\\n\\nThe maker of tur 8 did NOT apply this diff and did not edit KOSU-RABADON-2.md.\\nThe accompanying test is being written separately; until a human approves the\\ndiff above, the document and the tree still disagree, and this stays OPEN.\\n\",\"numLines\":68,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":68}}}\nreports/kosu/11.out.raw:13:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeMbnZvbLnCYNDdKjZFZ9\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01HjTPy6PgnBPLsrmyFCBrcJ\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"ls native/ | head -30; echo \\\"---\\\"; ls native/sock_path_test.sh 2>&1; echo \\\"---DENEMELER tail---\\\"; tail -30 reports/R7/DENEMELER.md\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":1544,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":4560,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":23960,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":4560},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f40cbadd-2bac-41b8-9a9c-9348aaba08b1\",\"uuid\":\"43a99439-94d1-4329-8750-bcb15b6ba875\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeMbnZ7j1GowbFGDR46RE\"}\nreports/kosu/11.out.raw:14:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01HjTPy6PgnBPLsrmyFCBrcJ\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"G1-PIPELINE.md\\nagents_test.sh\\narch_wrapper_test.sh\\nassign_prefix_test.sh\\naudit.cpp\\naudit_test.sh\\nbaseline.h\\nbaseline_t